{"t": 231.382, "n": 126, "ev": "result", "ok": true, "text": "I wrote the task rows for all seven phases, the proof table and the verification section into `plugins/tempergraph/docs/plans/i170c.plan.md`. Sections 0, 1 and 4, the phase goals and weights, and the status (`planned`) are as they were. I ran no tests and no git. The gate decides whether the rows are correct.\n\n- **Rows:** 34 rows in all, every Completed cell empty, since the plan had no rows before.\n  - **Requirements:** every requirement R1 to R13 is named by at least one row.\n  - **Docs row:** the one document under Docs to update, the improving-workflows guide, has its own row (7.1).\n  - **Test first:** each phase's test rows come before its code rows. Phase 7 has only the docs row, so test-first does not apply there.\n- **Code files opened:** I read every source file the code rows name before writing the row. The test files I opened were `test_filing.py`, `test_loop_issues.py`, `test_loop_issue_context.py`, `test_pause_findings_at_final_exit.py`, `test_stop_at_pause.py`, `test_release_watch.py` and `test_contract_tables.py`. For `test_improve.py` I read lines 320 to 360 only.\n- **New test files:** five are named by rows and do not exist yet. They are `test_outbox_delivery.py`, `test_outbox_verbs.py`, `test_pause_hand_on.py`, `test_operator_reason.py` and `test_segment_binding.py`.\n- **Proof table:** one row per task criterion (AC 1, 2, 3, 4, 6, 7, 8, 9), each with its test file. Every proof row uses the whole-suite command. I kept to the three declared commands (`python -m pytest`, `ruff check src tests`, `mypy`, each after `cd plugins/tempergraph/engine`). The `Proves` cells carry both the spec criterion id and the task's `AC n`, so a gate that matches either finds it.\n- **Pin checks:** I searched the tests that the changes could break and wrote the results into each phase.\n  - **Rows added:** the tests whose asserted fact changes (rows 2.1, 2.2, 3.3, 3.4, 5.1 and 5.2) each got a row.\n  - **No row needed:** no existing test needed a change for the `fault`-only pattern count, for `test_contract_tables.py` (the outbox verbs are sub-verbs of `improve`), or for `test_loop_child.py`'s `loop_started` checks.\n\nI added a few mechanisms the plan and specs do not spell out. The design itself is unchanged.\n- **Row 3.6:** a queued create keeps a pre-built `comment` body, so a later delivery as a comment carries the same context.\n- **Row 5.4:** the `loop_started` record gains a `held` flag, which is how a held child is told from one that dealt with its findings.\n- **Row 6.4:** the `--reason` value is checked through argparse `choices`, which already exits 2 before any write.\n\nI found no defect in the plan or the specs that blocks expanding it.\n\nARTIFACT phases: plugins/tempergraph/docs/plans/i170c.plan.md", "subtype": "success", "is_error": false, "session_id": "1e7d27c8-e6e7-48a0-8cc6-cc77a1c08220"}
